<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51328" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰσχνότης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ητος</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>thinness, leanness</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σαρκός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
				</span></i>
			<i>Aër.</i><i><span class="en">
				21
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σώματος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					581b26
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φύσιος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aret.
					<u>SA</u>
					1.7
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of style,
				<i>spareness</i>, i.e. <i>plainness</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰ. φράσεως</span>, of Lysias, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Vett.Cens.</u>
				5.1
			</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1.165S.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Demetr.
				<u>Eloc.</u>
				14
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>thinness, weakness</i> of pronunciation, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλατειασμός</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Quint.
				1.5.32
			</span></i>.</div>
